WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.340
A cold virus sits on a light switch.

2
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.660
For many hours, it does nothing on its own.

3
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.340
A fingertip can still pick it up.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.020
Inside your nose, it gets some of your cells to build new copies of it.

5
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.700
So what makes something alive?

6
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.220
Do bacteria and viruses pass the test?

7
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:28.753
Biologists check a list of characteristics.

8
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:32.553
Living things are made of one or more cells.

9
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:35.353
They take in and use energy.

10
00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:39.233
The chemical reactions that do this are called metabolism.

11
00:00:40.213 --> 00:00:44.633
They grow, respond, and keep their inside conditions steady.

12
00:00:45.493 --> 00:00:48.993
They reproduce, and they change over many generations.

13
00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:52.173
No single box decides it.

14
00:00:52.173 --> 00:00:57.513
A mature red blood cell cannot divide, but it is still a living cell.

15
00:00:58.453 --> 00:01:02.433
A crystal gets bigger, but it has no cells and no metabolism.

16
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:05.413
Now test a bacterium.

17
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:10.893
It is a prokaryote: a living thing made of one cell with no nucleus.

18
00:01:11.893 --> 00:01:16.453
In a damp place with food, it takes in nutrients and uses energy.

19
00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:19.953
It grows. It responds to its surroundings.

20
00:01:20.893 --> 00:01:23.493
Then it splits in two, all by itself.

21
00:01:24.353 --> 00:01:27.473
It has its own ribosomes, the parts that build proteins.

22
00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:30.513
So a bacterium is a living cell.

23
00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:39.267
Now test a virus. A virus is a tiny infectious agent: genetic material inside a

24
00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:42.907
protein coat. That coat is called a capsid.

25
00:01:43.707 --> 00:01:47.427
A virus is not a cell, and it has no ribosomes of its own.

26
00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:52.627
Outside a cell, it does not take in food, use energy, or grow.

27
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.380
A host cell is the living cell that a virus infects.

28
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.900
Inside it, the virus's genes get the cell to build new virus parts.

29
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.220
The parts come together as new viruses.

30
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.480
The cell does the building.

31
00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.660
The virus has no metabolism of its own.

32
00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:17.633
So the SOL classes viruses as nonliving.

33
00:02:18.353 --> 00:02:25.013
A virus is not a cell, it has no metabolism of its own, and it is copied only inside

34
00:02:25.013 --> 00:02:31.073
a host cell. Most bacteria carry out life processes by themselves when conditions

35
00:02:31.073 --> 00:02:34.533
suit them. Scientists still discuss the question.

36
00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:41.333
Keep this rule: bacteria are living cells, and viruses are classed as nonliving.
